XPU: graph-capturable TP collectives via torch symmetric memory
(VLLM_XPU_SYMM_AR=1). FALLBACK for oneCCL < 2022.1.2.

oneCCL 2022.1.1 (the version torch==2.14.0+xpu pins) cannot record
collectives into XPU (SYCL) graphs: capture either fails ("ext_oneapi_get_graph()
can only be called on recording queues") or silently records a broken graph.
oneCCL 2022.1.2 records correctly; use that when you can (it is what vLLM's
docker/Dockerfile.xpu installs). This patch is for stacks stuck on 2022.1.1.

While a graph is being captured, all_reduce, all_gather and gather stage the
input in a torch XPUSymmetricMemory buffer, synchronize with device-side
barrier kernels and read the peers' buffers over P2P -- ordinary recordable
kernels, ~16 us per all-reduce on replay (same as oneCCL 2022.1.2 in-graph).
Eager calls keep oneCCL. all_gather/gather matter for MTP: the drafter's FULL
prefill graph includes compute_logits, whose vocab-parallel gather otherwise
poisons every draft.

